ssion test.\n- [x] H200 kernel/cache and output-equivalence experiments pass.\n- [x] No documentation change is needed for this internal JIT behavior.\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\nPlease run the standard CUDA kernel CI for the added registered test.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40506193104](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40506193104)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40506193052](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40506193052)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40506193018](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40506193018)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n\n## Independent validation on the available H200\n\nThe available H200 NVL was also used for an independent validation with the local source snapshots. The environment for the output comparison and cache experiment was PyTorch 2.14.0+cu130 with Triton 3.8.0. With the same seeded BF16/FP32 inputs, the original and patched kernels produced byte-identical outputs:\n\n```text\nbuf        equal=True  max_abs=0.0  nonzero_diff=0\ntail_k     equal=True  max_abs=0.0  nonzero_diff=0\ntail_score equal=True  max_abs=0.0  nonzero_diff=0\n```\n\nFor widths 1, 2, 11, and 17, the original produced 4 Triton cache entries and took 2.7885 s for the first sequence; the patched version produced 1 entry and took 0.7870 s. The totals include first-use JIT compilation; subsequent patched widths took 0.0002--0.0005 s each. The registered CUDA regression test also passed in the available SGLang environment (PyTorch 2.13.0+cu130, Triton 3.7.1): `1 passed` in 9.26 s.\n\n",
